| 5 | `#dM` | `b#` | M[M,b] | `M::=@` |
| 6 | `#d` | `b#` | top `d` ≠ lookahead `b` | *(blank)* |

`出错：分析栈顶的“d”与当前输入符号“b”无法匹配` → `字符串aab不是该文法的句子` ✔

Relevant to Q3: step 5 does use a FOLLOW-derived cell, but via the *genuine* member `b ∈ Follow(M)` (from `M::=Ab`), not via the seeded `'#'`. The seeded `'#'` never gets a chance here because the input still has `b` pending. The rejection is structural: `H::=aMd` has committed the parser to a trailing `d` that the input cannot supply.

### 3b. Grammar test1 — `E::=a|b|(T)  T::=EG  G::=,EG|@`, input `(a,a)`

```
                   (           )           ,           a           b           #
       E     E::=(T)                               E::=a       E::=b
       T      T::=EG                              T::=EG      T::=EG
       G                   G::=@     G::=,EG                               G::=@
```

`Follow(E)={#,),,}`, `Follow(T)={#,)}`, `Follow(G)={#,)}`; only `G` is nullable, so only `G::=@` consults FOLLOW → columns `)` and `#`.

| 步骤 | 分析栈 | 剩余输入串 | 查表 | 所用产生式 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `#E` | `(a,a)#` | M[E,(] | `E::=(T)` |
| 2 | `#)T(` | `(a,a)#` | match | `“(”匹配` |
| 3 | `#)T` | `a,a)#` | M[T,a] | `T::=EG` |
| 4 | `#)GE` | `a,a)#` | M[E,a] | `E::=a` |
| 5 | `#)Ga` | `a,a)#` | match | `“a”匹配` |
| 6 | `#)G` | `,a)#` | M[G,,] | `G::=,EG` |
| 7 | `#)GE,` | `,a)#` | match | `“,”匹配` |
| 8 | `#)GE` | `a)#` | M[E,a] | `E::=a` |
| 9 | `#)Ga` | `a)#` | match | `“a”匹配` |
| 10 | `#)G` | `)#` | M[G,)] (FOLLOW-derived) | `G::=@` |
| 11 | `#)` | `)#` | match | `“)”匹配` |
| 12 | `#` | `#` | 两栈同时到底 | *(blank)* |

`字符串(a,a)是该文法的句子` ✔ — note step 2/11: `E::=(T)` is pushed in reverse (`)`, `T`, `(`) so the `(` is on top and the `)` waits at the bottom, which is exactly what makes the bracket match work.

